config SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE
    bool "Shared PRF storage"
    help
      Shared storage used by the PRF (recovery) firmware.

if SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE

config SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE_IMPORT_STOCK
    bool "Import the stock firmware's shared PRF storage"
    depends on RNG
    help
      On boards whose recovery firmware is the stock one, which keeps its own
      shared PRF storage (FLASH_REGION_STOCK_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE), copy that
      entry into ours when our identity root key differs from it. The phone
      then sees one watch, with the same address and bonding, in both
      firmwares. The stock region is only read.

module = SERVICE_SHARED_PRF_STORAGE
module-str = Shared PRF storage
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_level"

endif
